I don't have access to your network environment and active directory credentials to test this script. However, I can provide you with an outline for writing a powershell script that meets your requirements. Here's how you could approach it:

1. Define variables for the domain and base folder path. You may also want to specify a log file location and a flag to enable or disable logging.

```powershell
$domain = "your-domain"
$baseFolderPath = "c:\path\to\folder"
